First, the stock is anchored to the $35 buyout price. Even after a dividend payment, that acquisition price could remain relevant, assuming the deal is still going forward.

Second, the company is expected to have around $32 per share in cash. Paying a $6 dividend might not push the stock lower. It could actually push it higher by demonstrating that the company can distribute 20% of your investment in cash and potentially another 80% if it chooses to.

